- bread()/getblk() in hammer2_io_getblk() may sleep for buffer
  space with h2io, chain and inode locks held while the buffer
  daemon writes hammer2 buffers through hammer2_strategy_write().

- fsck_hammer2 prints "zone.1 exceeds volume size" on a 2GB volume;
  confirm it is informational only.

- No dirty memory throttling (pfs_memory_wait/wakeup, lwinprog
  ref/wait).  Relevant for fsync-heavy stalls.

- hammer2_vfs_sync_pmp(): ip->vp read and vget(LK_NOWAIT) before
  taking ip->lock; small window against reclaim.

- sbin/hammer2 check_volume(): reject partitions overlapping the
  disklabel/MBR.  newfs_hammer2 on a partition at offset 64 of an
  fdisk -i disk overwrites the disklabel.

- Comments in sys/hammer2 referencing other systems; strip or reword.

- cmd_debug.c prints "DragonFly HAMMER2" as the partition type name.

- hammer2_mount(): if hammer2_init_volumes() succeeds without setting
  hmp->devvp, hammer2_unmount_helper() runs on an hmp that is not on
  hammer2_mntlist and has no vchain/fchain, iohash or locks set up
  (TAILQ_REMOVE on a list it is not on), and the opened devvpl is
  never closed nor freed since it was not moved to hmp->devvp_list.

- hammer2_lookup() holds dip shared across hammer2_inode_get(), which
  locks nip exclusive; a corrupted directory entry resolving to dip
  itself (nip == dip) self-deadlocks.

- Truncating a file with embedded data (<= 512 bytes) to 0 and
  extending it returns the old contents instead of zeroes, also
  across a sync: hammer2_truncbuf() drops the buffer but the inode's
  embedded data is not cleared, and hammer2_strategy_read() copies
  it back.
